   "claims": [
    "For instance, the five number summary on the statistics from the above example would tell you that there are only a few people that come close to the maximal salary of $30,000, but plenty of employees making $1,500.",
    "The cool thing is that there's also a nice way to visualize the 5 number summary: the so-called box and whisker plot.",
    "Formulas of 5 number summary In this section, we present the formulas you need to use to find each of the 5 number summaries for your dataset.",
    "Firstly, let's see how to find the 5 number summary on this plot.",
    "Remember, however, that the 5 number summary in statistics provides only a general idea of your dataset, so this data analysis is not as exact as we'd sometimes wish.",
    "It's high time we see how to find the 5 number summary of an arbitrary dataset.",
    "We begin the process of how to find the 5 number summary of our sequence from the simplest of the five values: minimum = a₁; and maximum = an.",
    "This means that if, for instance, we have seven numbers (i.e., n = 7), then the median will be equal to a₄ because this entry has three elements to the left (smaller) and three elements to the right (larger).",
    "However, if n is odd, say, n = 7, then they are the medians of a₁, a₂, a₃, a₄ and of a₄, a₅, a₆, a₇, respectively (i.e., the middle number is repeated in both sequences).",
    "In a second, we'll do just that and finally see the 5 number summary calculator in action!"
   ],
